## Getting started
{%- if kind == 'library' %}

{{ project_name }} is built by the project that consumes it: no setup or CI of its own. Formatting and checks:
`pre-commit install` once, then `pre-commit run --all-files`.
{%- else %}

Requires Python 3.11 or newer and Git.

```bash
./setup.sh                    # Windows: .\setup.ps1
source .venv/bin/activate     # Windows: .\.venv\Scripts\Activate.ps1
```

`setup.sh` creates `.venv`, installs the project with its development tools{% if kind == 'project' %} and csorchestrator{% endif %}, and installs the
pre-commit hooks.
{%- if kind == 'project' %}

csorchestrator: `setup.sh` installs the pinned version ({{ csorchestrator_version }}). Another one:
`./setup.sh --csorchestrator=<tag or branch>`; a local clone, editable: `./setup.sh --csorchestrator=../csorchestrator`
(Windows: `.\setup.ps1 -CsOrchestrator <...>`).

Run the recipe locally, regenerate the GitHub workflow after changing it:

```bash
python {{ project_name }}_project.py
python {{ project_name }}_project.py generate-github-workflow
```
{%- endif %}

Checks and tests:

```bash
pre-commit run --all-files
pytest                        # --run-all: every test, as CI; --run=<marker>: an opt-in group (tests/conftest.py)
```
{%- endif %}

The shared files (setup, checks, CI, agent rules) come from
[cs-project-template](https://github.com/cscosine/cs-project-template); to bring them to its latest version, on a
branch: `copier update --defaults`.
